            <ArticleTitle>[A man with a painful and swollen ankle].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>A6894</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 58-year-old male patient was referred to the dermatologist because of swelling and pain of his left ankle. Radiodiagnostic imaging revealed an osteodestructive tumor which after biopsy proved to be a chondrosarcoma. Malignancy should be in the differential diagnosis of chronic one-sided edema.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
